From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] thunderbolt: qcom: make host-router activation impossible

The Qualcomm host-router platform driver is not ready to touch hardware.
Remove the module parameter that could enable its incomplete activation path.
The working tree also removes the activation code and unused NHI coupling;
this patch records the minimum fence for patch-series consumers.

---
 drivers/thunderbolt/qcom_usb4_hr.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom_usb4_hr.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom_usb4_hr.c
index ec42f9126a3a..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom_usb4_hr.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/qcom_usb4_hr.c
@@ -77,11 +77,7 @@ struct qcom_usb4_hr {
 	bool started;
 };
 
-static bool activate;
-module_param(activate, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(activate,
-		 "enable experimental Qualcomm USB4 host-router activation (default: false)");
+static const bool activate;
 
 static int qcom_usb4_hr_init_interrupts(struct tb_nhi *nhi)
 {
